==Enemy==
Mini Angel Cyclone follows a similar formula to [[Mesocosmocyclone]] and [[Li'l Zyclone]], being a smaller and faster [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]] with fairly high health and a lot of damage (though not that high for a Cyclone) done from close range. Her attacks have a 25% chance to generate a level 1 [[Mini-Surge]] at 150-750, which can compound greatly with her fast attack rate as they chip units by flooding the entire stage with Mini-Surges, proving especially deadly to fragile units like [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]] and anything that had survived a lethal strike. Unlike Divine Cyclone, she has an annoyingly high knockback count (44), which allows her to reposition easily, but also means she is easy to hold back in spite of her extreme speed.

At the minimum '''200%''' buff she appears with in Zero Legends, Mini Angel Cyclone has '''577,776''' HP, '''8,888''' attack power, and '''1,777''' Mini-Surge damage.

==Strategy==
Mini Angel Cyclone's main weakness is her high knockback count which can prevent her from pushing. Using fast attacking units with high DPS can make fighting Mini Angel Cyclone much easier as they can juggle her. Of course, being an [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] enemy, [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] is your best bet at stalling her. Similar to other high-knockback enemies, using units with high DPH such as [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] or [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]], can cripple her health.

